{"$comment":"The board's single vendor identity table. lib/vendor.ts (marks and monograms), lib/vendorColors.ts (family colors) and scripts/gen-og.mjs (the share image) all resolve through this file and nowhere else; scripts/check-vendor-agreement.mjs proves the three agree on every payload row. Resolution reads the display name, the adapter name and the wire together, first matching rule wins, so a model measured through a gateway still carries its maker's identity. No family color equals the flagged amber (#e8a33d), which stays reserved for the flagged encoding everywhere. glyph is the ink that stays legible on the family color when the color fills a disc or a chip. Brand-sampled colors (2026-10-26): Zhipu #126ef6 is the blue of Zhipu's published logo vector; TypeSafe #e551ba is the magenta of TypeSafe's published favicon; Upstage #805cfb is the deep stop of Upstage's published gradient; Inception #6f9aa5 is a lightened take on the slate of Inception's published favicon, lifted so the color still reads on the board's dark ground; ProtectAI #5f31cd is the rim purple of the shield in ProtectAI's published org avatar. Families with a null logo publish no usable mark: the board shows the mono letter instead, credited to the provider named in the label.","fallback":{"color":"#8b98a5","glyph":"#0b0e12","key":"other","label":"Other","logo":null,"mono":null},"families":[{"color":"#d7e0e8","glyph":"#0b0e12","key":"openai","label":"OpenAI","logo":"openai","mono":null},{"color":"#d97757","glyph":"#f4f7fa","key":"anthropic","label":"Anthropic","logo":"anthropic","mono":null},{"color":"#8ab8ff","glyph":"#0b0e12","key":"google","label":"Google","logo":"googlegemini","mono":null},{"color":"#4a7dff","glyph":"#f4f7fa","key":"meta","label":"Meta","logo":"meta","mono":null},{"color":"#4fb3e3","glyph":"#0b0e12","key":"ibm","label":"IBM","logo":"ibm","mono":null},{"color":"#ff8a3d","glyph":"#0b0e12","key":"mistral","label":"Mistral AI","logo":"mistralai","mono":null},{"color":"#f0b429